<% page_title "Creator claims" %>

<div id="c-admin-artist-claims">
  <div id="a-index" class="fixed-width-container mx-auto">
    <h1 class="mb-2">Creator claims</h1>
    <p class="fineprint mb-6">
      A creator asking for a creator tag to be recognised as theirs. An approved claim
      gives its creator control over who sees the posts carrying that tag. The rule
      below (the tag is locked, and strips to the creator's Matrix name) is checked
      again when you approve; it is a precondition, not proof that the person is who
      they say. A <code>41chan_</code> tag needs no claim. Every decision is written
      to the mod log, visible to admins only.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-2">Waiting</h2>
    <%# Each table scrolls inside its own box, so a phone scrolls the table and not the page. %>
    <div class="overflow-auto mb-8">
    <table id="artist-claims" class="striped w-full">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Matrix account</th><th>Booru account</th><th>Filed</th><th>Rule now</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @pending.each do |claim| %>
          <tr id="artist-claim-<%= claim.id %>">
            <td><%= link_to claim.tag_name, artist_path(claim.artist) %></td>
            <td><%= link_to claim.creator_gallery.matrix_id, creator_gallery_path(claim.creator_gallery) %></td>
            <td>
              <% if claim.claimant %>
                <%= link_to_user claim.claimant %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="fineprint">not linked</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td><%= time_ago_in_words_tagged(claim.created_at) %></td>
            <td>
              <% if @refusals.nil? %>
                <span class="fineprint">cannot check</span>
              <% elsif @refusals[claim.id] %>
                <span class="fineprint"><%= @refusals[claim.id] %></span>
              <% else %>
                holds
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td class="space-y-2">
              <%= button_to "Approve", approve_admin_artist_claim_path(claim), method: :post, class: "button-primary" %>
              <%= form_with url: reject_admin_artist_claim_path(claim), method: :post, class: "flex items-center gap-2" do |f| %>
                <%= f.text_field :note, placeholder: "why (shown to admins)" %>
                <%= f.submit "Reject", class: "button-outline-danger" %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% if @pending.empty? %>
          <tr><td colspan="6" class="fineprint">Nothing waiting.</td></tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mb-2">Decided</h2>
    <div class="overflow-auto">
    <table id="artist-claims-decided" class="striped w-full">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Matrix account</th><th>Answer</th><th>By</th><th>When</th><th>Note</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @decided.each do |claim| %>
          <tr id="artist-claim-<%= claim.id %>">
            <td><%= claim.tag_name %></td>
            <td><%= link_to claim.creator_gallery.matrix_id, creator_gallery_path(claim.creator_gallery) %></td>
            <td><%= claim.status %></td>
            <td><%= claim.approver ? link_to_user(claim.approver) : "-" %></td>
            <td><%= claim.decided_at ? time_ago_in_words_tagged(claim.decided_at) : "-" %></td>
            <td><%= claim.note.presence || "-" %></td>
            <td>
              <% if claim.approved? %>
                <%= button_to "Withdraw", reject_admin_artist_claim_path(claim), method: :post, class: "button-outline-danger",
                      params: { note: "approval withdrawn" },
                      form: { data: { confirm: "Withdraw the approval of #{claim.tag_name}? Its creator loses control of those posts." } } %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% if @decided.empty? %>
          <tr><td colspan="7" class="fineprint">No decisions yet.</td></tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-8 mb-2">Original characters</h2>
    <p class="fineprint mb-4">
      A creator claiming <code>name_(their name)</code> as their own character. A name nobody had used (no posts, no wiki
      page, no alias) was approved when filed; the ones here waiting had history, so look first: a series that happens to
      share the creator's name, say. An approved claim gives its creator their character's wiki page and fixes its
      category at character; it changes nothing about who sees posts. Decisions are in the public mod log. A claim
      <em>held</em> for a name was given by moving an old <code>oc_</code> tag onto <code>name_(creator)</code>, decided by
      whoever approved the move, for a creator with no page yet: it is approved the moment their page is made.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-auto">
    <table id="character-claims" class="striped w-full">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Tag</th><th>Creator</th><th>Booru account</th><th>Status</th><th>When</th><th>Note</th><th>Rule now</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% (@character_pending + @character_decided).each do |claim| %>
          <tr id="character-claim-<%= claim.id %>">
            <td><%= link_to claim.tag_name, posts_path(tags: claim.tag_name) %></td>
            <td>
              <% if claim.creator_gallery %>
                <%= link_to "@#{claim.slug}", creator_gallery_path(claim.creator_gallery) %>
              <% else %>
                @<%= claim.slug %> <span class="fineprint">no creator page yet</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td>
              <% if claim.creator_gallery&.user %>
                <%= link_to_user claim.creator_gallery.user %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="fineprint">not linked</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td><%= claim.status %><%= " by #{claim.approver.name}" if claim.approver && (claim.approved? || claim.rejected? || claim.held?) %><%= " by its creator" if claim.released? %></td>
            <td><%= time_ago_in_words_tagged(claim.decided_at || claim.created_at) %></td>
            <td><%= claim.note.presence || "-" %></td>
            <td>
              <% if !claim.pending? && !claim.approved? %>
                -
              <% elsif @character_refusals.nil? %>
                <span class="fineprint">cannot check</span>
              <% elsif @character_refusals[claim.id] %>
                <span class="fineprint"><%= @character_refusals[claim.id] %></span>
              <% else %>
                rule holds
              <% end %>
              <% if claim.pending? && @character_waits[claim.id].present? %>
                <div class="character-claim-waits fineprint">waits because <%= @character_waits[claim.id].to_sentence %></div>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td class="space-y-2">
              <% if claim.pending? %>
                <%= button_to "Approve", approve_admin_artist_claim_path(claim, kind: "character"), method: :post, class: "button-primary" %>
                <%= form_with url: reject_admin_artist_claim_path(claim, kind: "character"), method: :post, class: "flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" do |f| %>
                  <%= f.text_field :note, placeholder: "why (shown in the mod log)", size: 16 %>
                  <%= f.submit "Reject", class: "button-outline-danger" %>
                <% end %>
              <% elsif claim.approved? || claim.held? %>
                <%= button_to "Withdraw", reject_admin_artist_claim_path(claim, kind: "character"), method: :post, class: "button-outline-danger",
                      params: { note: "approval withdrawn" },
                      form: { data: { confirm: "Withdraw the approval of #{claim.tag_name}? Its creator loses the wiki page; the tag and the page stay." } } %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% if @character_pending.empty? && @character_decided.empty? %>
          <tr><td colspan="8" class="fineprint">No original character claims yet.</td></tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
